Now I have the full picture. Time to write the plan concretely.

## Plan

### A. `js/dfManager.js::isActiveRun` (CC 5, cov 0, CRAP 30)
Refactor:
```js
var ACTIVE_RUN_STATUSES = ['queued', 'pending', 'requested', 'waiting', 'in_progress'];

function isActiveRun(run) {
   return ACTIVE_RUN_STATUSES.indexOf(runStatus(run)) !== -1;
}
``
And export isActiveRun in module.exports for tests. Wait — "no code path removed"... adding to exports is additive; fine. Tests: each of 5 statuses → true; 'completed'/''/null/undefined-run/'SUCCESS' (case) → false; run without status → false. Characterization: isActiveRun(run) with status 'QUED'? runStatus lowercases → true.

### B. `js/common/checkRunZombies.js::classify` (CC 34, cov 95.9, CRAP 34.1)
Extract per-check-run decision into top-level named pure helpers:

```js
function zombieVerdict(cr, runId, reason) {
   return { kind: 'zombie', zombie: { name: (cr && cr.name) || null, runId: runId, reason: reason };
}
function liveVerdict(extra) → { kind: 'live', unresolvable: !!extra }
``

Helpers:
1. `classifyPendingRun(cr, runId, resolveRun, nowMs, graceMs)` — the linked-run half.
2. `verdictForResolvedRun(cr, runId, state, nowMs, graceMs)` — status vocabulary dispatch.
3. `verdictForCompletedRun(cr, runId, state, nowMs, graceMs)` — conclusion handling.
4. `verdictForConcludedRun(cr, runId, state, nowMs, graceMs)` — lag vs run-concluded.
5. `classifyUnlinkedRun(cr, nowMs, staleMs)` — stale-no-runner.

New `classify`:
```js
function classify(checkRuns, resolveRun, nowMs, opts) {
